invariant: INV-42
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_ifma_sign_model_test
reason: check_power returns after the check's public operation on AVX-512
  IFMA without rsa_ifma_sign_wipe_below, so the candidate signature in
  digits, which factors n when the check fails, stays in the dead frames
  of rsa_ifma.c's kernel. The verdict is the same.
  bin/rsa_ifma_sign_model_test counts the wipes and requires two from
  each signature on the kernels.

--- old
        rsa_vp1_cpu(cpu, k->n, k->n_len, candidate, power);
        rsa_ifma_sign_wipe_below();
--- new
        rsa_vp1_cpu(cpu, k->n, k->n_len, candidate, power);
